 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Not at all. It' kinder than pretending everything is fine when it's not. Say something like, I really want be there for you, but my allergies are really bad. Then ask if you can sit in the open air room near the door, and ask the caterer to keep allergies in mind. Nothing. Just a typical allergic question. We've all been asked it at some point. Weddings are beautiful rituals that don't need to stress everyone out. Try to relax and enjoy the atmosphere. Yes, carry a small box of clear plastic that opens at the front. People will usually ask before pushing in. You' not a burden. Just someone with a tough thing to deal with. Offer to help with the bathrooms so you' always near an exit.",
